## 10. Implement binding-site and interaction compatibility

A structurally similar ligand is not necessarily a suitable docking template. Add a binding-mode compatibility layer.

For every candidate ligand/PDB pair, calculate or retrieve:

- Contact residues.
- Contact residue overlap with known target pocket residues.
- Catalytic residue contacts.
- Hydrogen-bond donor/acceptor pattern.
- Hydrophobic contact pattern.
- Salt-bridge pattern.
- Aromatic stacking or cation–π interactions.
- Water-mediated contact information where available.
- Ligand exit-vector compatibility if computable.

For BACE1, make the active-site catalytic residues and substrate-recognition pocket configurable in target metadata. Do not hard-code them inside generic selection logic.

The score should reward conservation of important interactions:

\[
S_{\text{interaction}} =
w_c S_{\text{catalytic}}
+w_p S_{\text{pocket}}
+w_h S_{\text{hydrogenBond}}
+w_s S_{\text{saltBridge}}
+w_w S_{\text{waterNetwork}}
\]

The implementation should tolerate incomplete interaction metadata and report which terms were unavailable.

