## 12. Implement structure-quality scoring

Calculate a structure-quality score using available metadata.

Suggested components:

| Component | Suggested contribution |
|---|---:|
| Resolution | 20% |
| Binding-site completeness | 20% |
| Sequence coverage | 15% |
| Active-site integrity | 20% |
| Ligand occupancy/quality | 10% |
| Experimental method and refinement quality | 10% |
| MD preparation suitability | 5% |

Use configurable thresholds. Do not encode arbitrary thresholds without documenting them.

The quality score should penalize:

- Poor resolution.
- Missing active-site atoms.
- Severe chain breaks.
- Low ligand occupancy.
- Unresolved pocket residues.
- Major alternate conformations.
- Unusual geometry.
- Incompatible mutations.
- Incomplete catalytic residues.

The system should distinguish:

```text
qualityScore
qualityTier
qualityFlags
qualityWarnings
```

Example:

```json
{
  "qualityScore": 0.88,
  "qualityTier": "high",
  "qualityFlags": [],
  "qualityWarnings": [
    "One remote unresolved loop"
  ]
}
```

